  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, sorry you're having trouble. To help you quickly, could you tell us: 1) what isn't working (email, Teams, VPN, signing in, a printer, a specific app?), 2) any error message you see (a screenshot is great), and 3) when it started. One thing we noticed while checking: your mailbox is almost full (about 99%). If your problem is with email, for example messages won't send or Outlook won't sync, that's probably the cause. You can free up space by emptying Deleted Items and Junk Email, sorting your Inbox and Sent Items by size and deleting or saving big attachments to OneDrive, and turning on Online Archive for mail older than a year. The mailbox can take up to an hour to show the new size. Reply with more details and we'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket is vague ('it's not working'), no system named. lookup_user: Mei Chen (user 9), account active, 0 failed logins, not blocked, VPN enabled, password not expired. Mailbox at 99.4% (50890/51200 MB). This is the most likely cause if the issue is email; KB-010 says sending stops at 100%. Device BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15): online, recent check-in, 14.6% disk free, no warnings. Sent the user KB-010 cleanup steps and asked for details: what system, error text, when it started. No actions queued. If the mailbox is still over 95% after cleanup, escalate for a quota increase (needs manager approval).",
